{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q419103","formula":"Na₂Mg(SO₄)₂·4H₂O","hill":"H8MgNa2O12S2","elements":["H","O","Na","Mg","S"],"composition":{"H":8.0,"O":12.0,"S":2.0,"Mg":1.0,"Na":2.0},"names":{"en":"Blödite","ru":"Астраханит","uk":"Бльодит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Blödite or bloedite is a hydrated sodium magnesium sulfate mineral with the formula Na2Mg(SO4)2·4H2O. The mineral is clear to yellow in color often darkened by inclusions and forms monoclinic crystals. Blödite was first described in 1821 for an occurrence in a salt deposit in Ischler Salzberg, Bad Ischl, Gmunden, Austria and named for German mineralogist and chemist Karl August Blöde (1773–1820). It is found worldwide in evaporitic sedimentary environments such as the Great Salt Lake, Utah.","ru":"Астрахани́т (блёдит) — минерал, водный сульфат натрия и магния. Соль тёмного цвета, добываемая из астраханских солёных озёр хлорид-сульфатного типа и каспийского залива Кара-Богаз-Гол. Na2SO4·MgSO4·4H2O. Другое, общепринятое в наст.","uk":"Бльодит — мінерал, водний сульфат натрію і магнію. Інша назва — астраханіт."},"fame":17,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-559135","atoms":58,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[5.563,0.0,0.0],[0.0,8.366,0.0],[-2.009,0.0,11.043]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":4.598,"y":3.577,"z":1.532,"el":"Na"},{"x":3.593,"y":0.606,"z":7.053,"el":"Na"},{"x":-0.04,"y":7.76,"z":3.99,"el":"Na"},{"x":-1.044,"y":4.789,"z":9.511,"el":"Na"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Mg"},{"x":-2.009,"y":0.0,"z":11.043,"el":"Mg"},{"x":0.0,"y":8.366,"z":0.0,"el":"Mg"},{"x":-2.009,"y":8.366,"z":11.043,"el":"Mg"},{"x":5.563,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Mg"},{"x":3.554,"y":0.0,"z":11.043,"el":"Mg"},{"x":5.563,"y":8.366,"z":0.0,"el":"Mg"},{"x":3.554,"y"